      <h1>Chiropractor or Osteopath? <em>Training, Regulation and Benefit Categories in Canada</em></h1>
      <p>Chiropractors and osteopathic manual practitioners both treat back pain, neck pain and joint problems with manual care, and many clinics offer the two side by side. The professions still differ in ways that matter before you book.</p>
      <p>This guide compares their training, their legal status province by province, the way a visit runs, what each commonly treats, and how your extended health plan files the two under separate benefit categories.</p>
      <p class="byline">By WellFinder · November 2026 · 5 min read</p>
    </div>
      </div>

  </section>

